billion to repurchase its own shares and $974 million in dividends: $41.1 billion together (computed from two filed figures).","cites":["NVDA.buybacks.2026","NVDA.dividends.2026"]},{"topic":"quarter","text":"In the three months ended 2026-07-26 revenue was $96.2 billion, up 105.9% from $46.7 billion in the three months ended 2025-07-27.","cites":["NVDA.d.revenue.2026-04-27.2026-07-26","NVDA.d.revenue.2025-04-28.2025-07-27"]},{"topic":"ttm","text":"Over the four quarters to 2026-07-26 revenue added up to $303 billion (computed from five filed figures), operating income to $198 billion and net income to $193 billion.","cites":["NVDA.d.revenue.2025-07-28.2025-10-26","NVDA.d.revenue.2025-01-27.2026-01-25","NVDA.d.revenue.2025-01-27.2025-10-26","NVDA.d.revenue.2026-01-26.2026-04-26","NVDA.d.revenue.2026-04-27.2026-07-26","NVDA.d.opinc.2025-07-28.2025-10-26","NVDA.d.opinc.2025-01-27.2026-01-25","NVDA.d.opinc.2025-01-27.2025-10-26","NVDA.d.opinc.2026-01-26.2026-04-26","NVDA.d.opinc.2026-04-27.2026-07-26","NVDA.d.netinc.2025-07-28.2025-10-26","NVDA.d.netinc.2025-01-27.2026-01-25","NVDA.d.netinc.2025-01-27.2025-10-26","NVDA.d.netinc.2026-01-26.2026-04-26","NVDA.d.netinc.2026-04-27.2026-07-26"]},{"topic":"ttm","text":"Free cash flow over the same four quarters was $127 billion: operating cash flow of $134 billion less capital spending of $7.4 billion (computed from ten filed figures).","cites":["NVDA.d.ocf.2025-01-27.2025-10-26","NVDA.d.ocf.2025-01-27.2025-07-27","NVDA.d.ocf.2025-01-27.2026-01-25","NVDA.d.ocf.2026-01-26.2026-04-26","NVDA.d.ocf.2026-01-26.2026-07-26","NVDA.d.capex.2025-01-27.2025-10-26","NVDA.d.capex.2025-01-27.2025-07-27","NVDA.d.capex.2025-01-27.2026-01-25","NVDA.d.capex.2026-01-26.2026-04-26","NVDA.d.capex.2026-01-26.2026-07-26"]},{"topic":"pay","text":"The proxy statement filed 2026-05-12 gives the principal executive officer’s total pay for FY2026 as $36.3 million in its summary compensation table, and the “compensation actually paid” - the SEC’s measure, which revalues share awards over the year - as $162 million.","cites":["NVDA.pay.peoTotal.2026","NVDA.pay.peoPaid.2026"]},{"topic":"pay","text":"For the other named executive officers the same table gives an average of $14.4 million in total and $57.7 million actually paid.","cites":["NVDA.pay.neoTotal.2026","NVDA.pay.neoPaid.2026"]},{"topic":"pay","text":"The table puts the value of $100 held in the company’s shares over the years it covers at $1,445.67 at the end of FY2026, and $198.10 for the peer group the company chose.","cites":["NVDA.pay.tsr.2026","NVDA.pay.peerTsr.2026"]},{"topic":"backlog","text":"Remaining performance obligations - revenue under contract that was not yet recognised - were $2.3 billion at the end of FY2026, against $1.7 billion a year earlier. That is 1.1% of FY2026 revenue (computed from two filed figures).","cites":["NVDA.rpo.2026","NVDA.rpo.2025","NVDA.revenue.2026"]},{"topic":"backlog","text":"Deferred revenue was $2.6 billion at the end of FY2026 (tagged ContractWithCustomerLiability), against $1.8 billion a year earlier.","cites":["NVDA.deferred.2026","NVDA.deferred.2025"]},{"topic":"people","text":"The latest annual report gives the workforce as 42,000 in its own words. FY2026 revenue works out to about $5.1 million for each (computed from one filed figure and the number in that sentence).","cites":["NVDA.q.employees","NVDA.revenue.2026"]},{"topic":"debt","text":"At the end of FY2026 the balance sheet carried $10.6 billion in cash and cash equivalents, and $8.5 billion of debt as tagged (LongTermDebtNoncurrent + DebtCurrent). Cash exceeded that debt by $2.1 billion (computed from three filed figures).","cites":["NVDA.cash.2026","NVDA.debtLong.2026","NVDA.debtCurrent.2026"]}]},"fin":{"NVDA":{"insiders":{"from":"2025-11-23","to":"2026-11-23","complete":true,"listed":79,"read":79,"other":0,"failed":0,"odd":0,"people":[["Teter Timothy S.","EVP, General Counsel and Sec"],["STEVENS MARK A","Director"],["Kress Colette","EVP & Chief Financi